# Post-open-kan discard followed by a call (pon) still reveals the owed kan dora
# (engine.md §4.2 Kan transactions, rules.md §4.17, §5 item 4).
# Seat 0 discards 5z -> Seat 1 calls daiminkan on 5z (owes kan dora 7p -> dora 8p).
# Seat 1 draws rinshan 6z and discards 6z -> Seat 2 calls pon:66z and discards 9m!
# Both rulesets reveal 7p before dahai(1), ahead of pon(2).
# Seat 3 draws and discards 7s -> Seat 2 rons 7s with yakuhai_hatsu (1) + dora:2 (88p) = 3 han 30 fu = 3900!

[meta]
name: open_kan_discard_called_dora
title: Post-open-kan discard called by pon reveals the owed kan dora
rules: both
source: engine.md §4.2, rules.md §4.17, §5.4; real-log campaign, docs/notes/p3-reallogs.md

